00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.550
the Ashland Grizzlies,

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:09.720
and I've had them forever
and I just love them.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.070
And I think I'll always love them.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:14.590
- [Is] Someone just
really landed a hard ball.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:15.810
Are you happy?

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.030
- (laughing) Jesus...

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.110
Oh, man.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.000
It's like (feigned explosion),

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.159
point blank, deer-in-the-headlights.

00:20:23.159 --> 00:20:25.180
- (in slow motion) Headlights.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.560
- You know, am I happy?

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:31.700
Yes. I mean, I'm, the definition of happy,

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.330
when you live with singular experience,

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:34.830
you don't know what happy
is for other people.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:37.570
So I don't know, I-I'm
stressed about things.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:38.790
I'm worried about things.

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:41.850
I stress about the future
of my children's lives

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:43.130
and et cetera.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:48.020
But overall, I am happy
with the life that I have.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:50.740
And, and that's mainly because I have deep

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:53.200
beautiful relationships
with these people around me

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.970
that give a lot of meaning to my life.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:58.320
I think the work that I do
and the success that I've had

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:01.730
in this work is a, an
amplifier of that happiness.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.040
But I wouldn't say it's the core.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.780
I wouldn't say that it is the foundation.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:07.150
It is an amplifier.

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:08.650
I feel like a lot of external factors

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:10.170
that aren't relationship-based

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.760
can be amplifiers, but I, I'm not sure

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:15.590
that they can be the core because I see,

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:16.440
especially on YouTube

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:18.210
where there's algorithms
and some videos do well,

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.360
and some don't (sniffs),

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.420
if my happiness were founded
on, on, on this work,

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.960
it would be a roller coaster.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.970
And it is sometimes, if I
find myself investing too much

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.370
of my worth into this,
it is a roller coaster.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:34.620
And so I try to invest
in, in my relationships.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:37.340
And so, yeah, I would say
I'm happy, in a sense.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.210
- [Is] Do you have a team
helping you make videos

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.500
or is it just to you?

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.300
You seem to be able to create content

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.900
with exceptional quality in a short time.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:45.800
- I have a team.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.540
- And I'm putting together a special team.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:50.230
- For years, I've been
slowly training people

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:53.530
to think in the way that I think

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:54.900
when it comes to editing and then they've

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.450
added their own personalities
into it as well.

00:21:57.450 --> 00:21:59.400
And together that's created our style.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:02.030
I have a team that helps edit and animate,

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.920
and more and more will take
on the edits, start to finish.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.930
I won't be jumping in Premiere
nearly as much anymore

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:09.680
as I used to, or After Effects.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.550
Although at After Effects
I still do jump in

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:13.200
and play around because I love it.

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:15.850
I write, though. The writing
is the bottleneck for me.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:17.740
It's the thing that I, I do

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:19.770
and will probably always
do, to some degree,

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:21.150
because it, it's what I want to say

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:21.983
and how I want to say it.

00:22:21.983 --> 00:22:24.510
And I direct, I have a
whole scripting method

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:26.720
that I use to direct the visuals.

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:29.360
- [Is] That kind of
goes with this question,

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:31.540
which is, do you,

00:22:31.540 --> 00:22:34.170
do you have the animation
and editing in your mind

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:35.420
before the narration script?

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:36.820
- Yes, absolutely.

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:39.060
So when I'm writing a video,

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.821
and this is if you're on Patreon,

00:22:40.821 --> 00:22:43.090
I do, I publish all my scripts

00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:45.970
and also do behind the
scenes on all this stuff.

00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:47.820
So, Patreons, thank you, Patreons.

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:51.400
I have the vision of everything
in my head as I'm writing,

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:53.070
and then editors and animators

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:56.770
who work on my videos will
add their own interpretation.

00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:59.020
They'll add their own
version of what I put.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:00.240
Often, it's super specific,

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:01.490
so they'll put in what I put,

00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:03.710
but then other times it's like, they,

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:04.870
it's open to interpretation

00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:06.380
and they put in whatever they feel.

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:07.213
So it's a balance there,

00:23:07.213 --> 00:23:08.910
but I absolutely, for certain visuals,

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:10.640
have a very specific vision

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:12.070
that I write into these scripts.

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:14.130
- [Is] How do you simplify complex stories

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:15.830
and express it with so much ease?

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:18.690
Was this something
built, like built in you

00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:20.000
or have you worked on it?

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.280
- I've definitely worked on this craft

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:24.720
of explaining complicated things.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:27.670
What you need to know is that
when I'm writing a piece,

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:30.150
I am wrestling with the explanation.

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:32.180
I'm wrestling with every single word

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.250
because I know that
when you're watching it,

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:36.720
those words are coming by
at a million miles an hour.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:38.803
Your brain's either going
to ingest them or...

00:23:38.803 --> 00:23:39.636
(snaps fingers)
...it's not.

00:23:39.636 --> 00:23:41.900
And if it's not, you're not
going to pause and rewind.

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:42.860
You're just going to move onc and be like,

00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:43.693
I didn't get that.

00:23:43.693 --> 00:23:45.840
So I'm thinking, I need
to make sure every word

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:47.800
that comes out of my mouth is worthy

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:49.020
of this person's (chuckling) brain.

00:23:49.020 --> 00:23:50.810
It will sink in and they'll understand.

00:23:50.810 --> 00:23:51.850
And so, I'll go over it.

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:54.410
And I'll even belabor
the explanation over,

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:55.670
and repeat myself sometimes

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:57.340
in the name of, of understanding.

00:23:57.340 --> 00:23:59.420
I think it's natural in me

00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:01.000
because I've always been someone

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.860
who wants to teach and explain.

00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:05.780
But again, I'm very dyslexic and, that,

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:07.630
I struggled big time in
school because of that.

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:10.062
And so, I always wished
someone would explain it to me.

00:24:10.062 --> 00:24:12.710
Once I found out what a black hole was

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:16.067
or what a cell was, I was,
once I found that out,

00:24:16.067 --> 00:24:17.870
and understood it in like my adulthood,

00:24:17.870 --> 00:24:18.703
I was like, oh, it
wasn't that complicated.

00:24:18.703 --> 00:24:22.260
I spent 20 years of my life

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:24.050
feeling like I couldn't
understand anything.

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:26.150
And it's because it was words on a page.

00:24:26.150 --> 00:24:28.210
And so, all I needed was this visual.

00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:29.740
This visual helps me understand it.

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:31.160
And this really good explanation.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:34.800
And so, I think I have built a whole world

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:37.540
out of trying to explain things in the way

00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:38.790
I wish someone had explained it to me.

00:24:38.790 --> 00:24:40.630
That, that summarizes a lot of my style.

00:24:40.630 --> 00:24:42.170
So it's very innate in that way

00:24:42.170 --> 00:24:45.480
but it's also wrought from
a desire to explain things

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:46.313
in a way that someone can understand it.

00:24:46.313 --> 00:24:48.440
Because I hate the feeling
of not understanding,

00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:49.530
I hate that feeling.

00:24:49.530 --> 00:24:50.667
And that someone's smarter than me

00:24:50.667 --> 00:24:53.210
and that they are using
their understanding

00:24:53.210 --> 00:24:55.030
to brandish that. It's not a good feeling.

00:24:55.030 --> 00:24:56.290
I feel like there's so much of that.

00:24:56.290 --> 00:24:57.850
And it's like, let's let everyone

00:24:57.850 --> 00:25:00.200
just understand this thing.

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:01.910
- [Is] I was going to ask
if you had a pet peeve,

00:25:01.910 --> 00:25:02.810
but...
- (laughs)

00:25:02.810 --> 00:25:05.078
- [Is] ...it sounds like
we just heard all about it.

00:25:05.078 --> 00:25:06.003
- (laughing) Geez.

00:25:06.850 --> 00:25:08.320
Thank you all for being here.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:10.350
Thank you, Patreons.

00:25:10.350 --> 00:25:12.980
Thank you Policygenius
for supporting this video.

00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:15.810
And I, next time you see me,

00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:17.860
I will, I will be in a
completely different scenario.

00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:20.130
We have so many cool
videos coming up in June

00:25:20.130 --> 00:25:21.370
about really cool stuff.

00:25:21.370 --> 00:25:22.480
And I'm excited to share them with you.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:24.460
But for now I'm going to go take a nap.

00:25:24.460 --> 00:25:27.740
- [Is] If you had any questions
that you didn't answer,

00:25:27.740 --> 00:25:29.820
leave them in the comments so
he can answer them next time.

00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:31.770
- That's a good, good point.
- [Is] (laughs)

00:25:31.770 --> 00:25:34.120
- [Johnny] Bye, everybody.
(laughter)

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:35.483
- Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:25:36.760 --> 00:25:40.523
I'm going to hurl.
